components.design:
DATA MODEL (data/store.js). Persisted to store.json via atomic temp+rename, mode 0600:
  users: { id, name, email, emailVerified, emailVerifiedAt, password (scrypt$v$N$r$p$pepperVer$salt$hash), inviteCode, inviteCodeExpires, inviteCodeUses, dob, isAdmin, status: 'active'|'disabled'|'pending'|'deleted', sharingPausedUntil, createdAt, updatedAt, deletedAt }
  emailTokens: { id, userId, kind: 'verify'|'reset', digest, expires, usedAt }
  sessions: digest -> { userId, csrfToken, createdAt, lastSeenAt, idleExpires, absoluteExpires, uaHash, ipPrefixHash, label }
  friendRequests: { id, fromId, toId, status: 'pending'|'accepted'|'declined'|'cancelled'|'expired', source: 'code'|'email', createdAt, respondedAt, declineCount }
  friendships: { id, userA, userB (canonical userA<userB), createdAt }
  blocks: { id, blockerId, blockedId, reason, createdAt }
  reports: { id, reporterId (or pseudonym hash), subjectId, category, note, context, status, createdAt, reviewedAt, reviewerNote }
  shares: `${ownerId}:${viewerId}` -> { createdAt, expiresAt, precision: 'exact'|'area'|'city', createdBySessionId, lastViewedAt, viewCount }
  checkins: { id, userId, placeId, placeName, lat, lng, note, createdAt, expiresAt }
  savedPlaces: { id, userId, placeId, name, category, createdAt } (validated, 500/user)
  apiUsage: { date, nearby, place, geocode, perUser: { userId: {...} }, month, monthTotals }
  placeCache / nearbyCache: keyed lookups with TTL (may live in memory or a separate file; must not bloat store.json)
IN-MEMORY ONLY, never persisted:
  locations: Map userId -> { lat, lng, accuracy, updatedAt, expiresAt }
  locationAccess: Map ownerId -> bounded ring buffer of { viewerId, at }
  rateBuckets, loginAttempts, hashSemaphore queue (all bounded/LRU)
INDEXES rebuilt at load and on mutation: usersById, usersByEmail, usersByInviteCode, friendsByUser (Map<id, Set<id>>), blocksByUser.

ENDPOINTS. Every non-GET requires: session + Origin/Sec-Fetch-Site check + exact application/json + X-CSRF-Token.
Auth/account: POST /api/auth/signup (202 always) | GET /api/auth/verify?token | POST /api/auth/verify/resend | POST /api/auth/login | POST /api/auth/logout | POST /api/auth/logout-all | GET /api/auth/me | POST /api/auth/password/forgot (202 always) | POST /api/auth/password/reset | POST /api/auth/password/change | GET /api/auth/sessions | DELETE /api/auth/sessions/:id | GET /api/account/export | POST /api/account/delete
Friends: GET /api/friends | GET /api/friends/invite | POST /api/friends/invite/rotate | POST /api/friends/request {code|email} (202 always, identical for success/nonexistent/blocked/cooldown) | POST /api/friends/accept | POST /api/friends/decline {requestId, block?} | POST /api/friends/cancel | POST /api/friends/remove | POST /api/friends/block | POST /api/friends/unblock | GET /api/friends/blocked | POST /api/report
Location: POST /api/location/share {friendId, durationMin<=480, precision} | DELETE /api/location/share?friendId= | POST /api/location/stop-all | POST /api/location/pause {untilMs} | GET /api/location/audience | GET /api/location/access-log | POST /api/location {lat,lng,accuracy} (409 when no active share) | DELETE /api/location | GET /api/friends/locations (expiry-filtered, per-viewer precision, minute-rounded timestamps)
Check-ins: POST /api/checkins {placeId, note, durationMin} | GET /api/checkins | DELETE /api/checkins/:id
Saved: GET /api/saved | POST /api/saved (validated) | DELETE /api/saved?id=
Search: POST /api/nearby | POST /api/geocode | GET /api/place?id= (session-gated, cached, per-user sub-cap) | GET /api/config
Admin: GET /api/admin/reports | POST /api/admin/reports/:id | POST /api/admin/users/:id/disable

RESPONSE INVARIANTS TO ENFORCE IN CODE REVIEW:
1. No endpoint ever confirms or denies the existence of an account to a party who does not already have a relationship with it (signup, forgot-password and friend-request all answer 202 identically, in constant time).
2. No response body ever contains another user's email address.
3. Every read of another user's data passes through one canSee(viewer, subject) function that defaults to deny.
4. /api/friends/locations returns nothing for an expired share, an expired point, a block, a paused user, or a disabled account — checked server-side, never client-side.
5. Location is never written to disk.
6. Every location share has a non-null expiresAt <= 8 hours out.
